          "clarity_and_justification": true,
          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly queried APPROVED_PENDING work orders (site MAIN, Transformer 1, page_size=0), found none, retrieved the latest DGA reading, and applied the no-pending fallback by stating so and advising on a new work order. However, fmsr.interpret_dga returned 'LLM unavailable' and the agent neither retried nor disclosed this failure; it silently substituted a manual classification and labelled it 'reliable'. The manual IEC 60599 coding is also wrong: CH4/H2 = 2.6 (>1) should be code 2, C2H2/C2H4 ≈ 0 code 0, C2H4/C2H6 = 3.04 (1–4) code 1, giving T2 (thermal fault 300–700 °C), not '1-0-1 = 150–300 °C'. The agent should have retried the tool, transparently reported the failure, and applied the IEC ratio limits correctly. The remark that acetylene at 7 ppm suggests discharge is also weak given C2H2/C2H4 is negligible; acetylene relevance here is only for the priority-escalation rule, which was not applicable."
